{:edb/db-before-t 5231 :edb/db-after-t 5232 :edb/tx-data [[13194139538544 50 #inst "2026-10-21T00:42:40.855Z" 13194139538544 17592186576411 true] [17592186054624 1038 #edb/ref 17592186670718 13194139538544 17592186576411 true] [17592186054624 1038 #edb/ref 17592186670719 13194139538544 17592186576411 true] [17592186054624 1038 #edb/ref 17592186670720 13194139538544 17592186576411 true] [17592186054624 1040 #edb/ref 17592186608313 13194139538544 17592186576411 false] [17592186054624 1040 #edb/ref 17592186670717 13194139538544 17592186576411 true] [17592186608285 1173 true 13194139538544 17592186576411 true] [17592186608296 1173 true 13194139538544 17592186576411 true] [17592186608299 1074 "Using the quotient rule and then the product rule for logarithms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln\\left(\\frac{q\\cdot 2}{e}\\right) &= \\ln\\left(q\\cdot 2\\right)-\\ln\\left(e\\right) \\\\ &= -\\ln\\left(e\\right)+\\ln\\left(2\\right)+\\ln\\left(q\\right) \\\\ &= -1+\\ln\\left(2\\right)+\\ln\\left(q\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere $\\ln\\left(e\\right)=1$." 13194139538544 17592186576411 false] [17592186608299 1074 "Using the quotient rule for logarithms, separate the numerator and denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\ln\\left(\\frac{q\\cdot 2}{e}\\right) \\\\ &=\\ln\\left(q\\cdot 2\\right)-\\ln\\left(e\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow use the product rule to expand the logarithm of the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\ln\\left(q\\cdot 2\\right)-\\ln\\left(e\\right) \\\\ &=\\ln\\left(q\\right)+\\ln\\left(2\\right)-\\ln\\left(e\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\ln\\left(e\\right)=1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\ln\\left(q\\right)+\\ln\\left(2\\right)-\\ln\\left(e\\right) \\\\ &=\\ln\\left(q\\right)+\\ln\\left(2\\right)-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139538544 17592186576411 true] [17592186608300 1173 true 13194139538544 17592186576411 true] [17592186608308 1074 "Using the product rule for logarithms, combine the first two terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\log\\left(9\\right)+\\log\\left(z\\right)-\\log\\left(x\\right) \\\\ &=\\log\\left(9\\cdot z\\right)-\\log\\left(x\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow use the quotient rule to combine the remaining difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\log\\left(9\\cdot z\\right)-\\log\\left(x\\right) \\\\ &=\\log\\left(\\frac{9\\cdot z}{x}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139538544 17592186576411 true] [17592186608308 1074 "Using the product rule, combine the logarithms with the same sign. Then use the quotient rule to subtract the denominator logarithm:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\log\\left(9\\right)+\\log\\left(z\\right)-\\log\\left(x\\right) &= \\log\\left(9\\cdot z\\right)-\\log\\left(x\\right) \\\\ &= \\log\\left(\\frac{9\\cdot z}{x}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139538544 17592186576411 false] [17592186608313 1168 "generators/2b/2b85d4e47d7b57e56322672f222d5e2f3d395708c5cd3ebc3222ab720c56644e/generator.py" 13194139538544 17592186576411 true] [17592186670699 1080 "\\ln\\left(\\frac{9\\cdot q}{p}\\right)" 13194139538544 17592186576411 true] [17592186670699 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538544 17592186576411 true] [17592186670699 1083 #uuid "1456845d-d8fd-5cc6-93da-e9af372cef13" 13194139538544 17592186576411 true] [17592186670700 1080 "\\ln\\left(\\frac{5}{x\\cdot z}\\right)" 13194139538544 17592186576411 true] [17592186670700 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538544 17592186576411 true] [17592186670700 1083 #uuid "211e3c76-2477-5f6f-b432-2f71d4ab5237" 13194139538544 17592186576411 true] [17592186670701 1080 "\\ln\\left(\\frac{5\\cdot x}{z}\\right)" 13194139538544 17592186576411 true] [17592186670701 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538544 17592186576411 true] [17592186670701 1083 #uuid "217eb422-cb2c-5579-8158-d7a300e7a17d" 13194139538544 17592186576411 true] [17592186670702 1080 "1-\\ln\\left(p\\right)-\\ln\\left(3\\right)" 13194139538544 17592186576411 true] [17592186670702 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538544 17592186576411 true] [17592186670702 1083 #uuid "6c